    scene bg CLASSROOM

    no "I got to the classroom and forcibly swung the door open. Everyone heard it crashing against the wall, so they all turned to look at me in unison. I hated it. I hated their ugly stares and their midwit brains all coming together to judge me the same way they do Sharlene."

    ca "G... Good morning, Sofia..."

    cb "Hey, don't say morning to her―"

    no "They stopped because they knew I heard them whispering. I shot them a glare after all. The group shuffles around in their seats awkwardly. They're treating me like some kind of murderer bitch, even though I knew well that they wouldn't give a rats ass if I killed that Shokoy. Hell, I knew they might even be happy about it if I tried. It didn't matter. All I knew was that I really really wanted to leave. The girls started forming a small ring of gossip in the middle of the classroom, and the boys, uncaring and playing games on their phones, visibly inched themselves closer just to see if they could get any laughs in talking about the crazy bitch. They didn't understand a thing. I knew they didn't. So it didn't matter."

    no "I swung the door open as loud as I could, again, just to make sure everyone knew."

